  <!--
    Indonesian (id) resources.

    Two kinds of entry live here:
      1. Enum display names, keyed synthetically ("PaymentType_Cash") — see SharedResource.resx.
      2. UI chrome and explanatory prose, keyed by the ENGLISH TEXT ITSELF.

    Anything not listed here falls back to its key, i.e. renders as English. That is
    deliberate and is what makes the phased rollout safe — an untranslated string is
    readable English, never blank or a raw key.

    NOT in this file, on purpose: Indonesian domain/accounting terms (PPN, DPP, HPP,
    Laba Kotor, Laba Usaha, Laba Bersih, Piutang, Utang, Retur Penjualan, Nota Kredit…).
    Those stay Indonesian in BOTH languages because they are the terms staff, the tax
    consultant and the printed paperwork already use — so they are left as bare literals
    in the markup and never routed through the localizer at all.
  -->
